      "problem": "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}=1?$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{5}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=0$ and $k=3.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(0,3).$",
